{
  "$comment": [
    "Declarative selection of BodyParts3D 4.0 element files for the Skeleton Viewer V1 model.",
    "Most ids here come from the official PART-OF mapping tables shipped with the dataset:",
    "  partof_parts_list_e.txt      concept id (FMA) -> representation id (BP) -> English name",
    "  partof_element_parts.txt     concept id (FMA) -> element file id (FJ*.obj)",
    "Cranial nerve ids come from the official IS-A mapping tables because the PART-OF archive does not include those nerve OBJ files:",
    "  isa_parts_list_e.txt         concept id (FMA) -> representation id (BP) -> English name",
    "  isa_element_parts.txt        concept id (FMA) -> element file id (FJ*.obj)",
    "\"source\": \"isa\" selects the ISA OBJ archive; omitted means PART-OF.",
    "The FMA concepts chosen are the explicitly sided ones, so left/right identity comes from the",
    "official metadata rather than from geometry inspection. The build script additionally checks",
    "the representation id recorded inside each OBJ header and the sign of each mesh centroid.",
    "\"system\": \"skeletal\" | \"organ\" | \"nervous\" | \"nerve\" selects which GLTF material a mesh gets (see build-bodyparts3d-skeleton.mjs)."
  ],
